# E §3.1 The order of the checks (tally 2.1.2, issue #23): the passes run in order, and the first pass that refuses
# prints, whatever the lines. The def's value at line 11 is no id (LOAD-KEY, pass 4, the items' own checks); the unit
# declared again at line 15 is LOAD-DUP (pass 2, the declarations), which prints.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "a source"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

def fee: money PLN = rate

ask q: fee

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
=== expect
refused: LOAD-DUP ...
